  "body": "Currently, there is [no bulletproof way to monitor caret position](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/10657161/is-it-possible-watch-the-caret-position-in-a-textarea-without-polling/10657305) without polling or listening to a large number of events.\r\n\r\n* There is the `select` event, but only monitors user action that results to a selection\r\n* Authors would need to also listen to `pointerdown`, `pointerup`, `keydown`, `keyup` etc to catch all caret position changes, and I suspect there are still edge cases where they are not sufficient.\r\n\r\nAlso, it requires complicated heuristics to distinguish an actual caret position change (e.g. through clicking or using arrow keys) from the caret just moving naturally as the user is entering text.\r\n\r\nAlso, none of these capture \"artificial\" caret position changing, by using `selectionStart`, `setSelectionRange()` etc.\r\n\r\n",
